                "Retaliation: The infuriated mob chased the police into the police station and set it on fire, resulting in the death of 22 policemen.",
                "Gandhi's Reaction: Deeply anguished by the violence, Gandhi declared that the nation was not yet adequately trained in non-violence and called an emergency meeting of the Congress Working Committee at Bardoli.",
                "Bardoli Resolution (February 12, 1922): The CWC formally suspended the Non-Cooperation Movement and directed all Congressmen to engage exclusively in constructive work (charkha, eradication of untouchability, national schools).",
                "Severe criticism: National leaders imprisoned in British jails (Subhas Chandra Bose, Jawaharlal Nehru, C.R. Das, Motilal Nehru, Lala Lajpat Rai) expressed bitter shock and dismay at the sudden unilateral suspension.",
