                "Delhi Special Session (Sept 1923, chaired by Maulana Azad) permitted Congressmen to contest elections while preserving Congress unity.",
                "Electoral Success (Nov 1923 elections): Swarajists won 42 out of 101 elected seats in the Central Legislative Assembly, emerged as the single largest party in Bengal and Central Provinces.",
                "Key Swarajist achievements: Defeated government budgets, exposed dyarchy, forced appointment of the Muddiman Committee (1924) on constitutional reforms, and elected Vitthalbhai Patel as the first Indian Speaker (President) of the Central Legislative Assembly in 1925.",
