            "theoryHtml": "\n<div class='module-content'>\n    <h4>1. Resurgence of Armed Struggle in Northern India</h4>\n    <p>The abrupt calling off of the Non-Cooperation Movement in 1922 created acute ideological disillusionment among the youth who had sacrificed their careers. Influenced by the Russian Revolution of 1917, Marxist literature, and the militant working-class uprisings across Europe, young revolutionaries resolved to organize an armed rebellion to overthrow British rule.</p>\n\n    <h4>2. Foundation of HRA (Kanpur, October 1924)</h4>\n    <p>In October 1924, young patriots assembled at Kanpur and founded the <strong>Hindustan Republican Association (HRA)</strong>. Key founders included <strong>Ram Prasad Bismil</strong>, <strong>Sachindra Nath Sanyal</strong>, and <strong>Jogesh Chandra Chatterjee</strong>.</p>\n    <ul>\n        <li>Their manifesto, <em>'The Revolutionary'</em> (January 1925), declared the objective of establishing a <em>Federal Republic of the United States of India</em> based on universal adult franchise.</li>\n        <li>It explicitly avowed socialist ideals, demanding the nationalization of railways, heavy industries, and financial institutions.</li>\n        <li>Sachindra Nath Sanyal's book <em>'Bandi Jiwan'</em> inspired thousands of youngsters, including Bhagat Singh.</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <h4>3. The Kakori Train Action (August 9, 1925)</h4>\n    <p>Facing an acute shortage of funds to procure arms, ten HRA revolutionaries executed a meticulously planned raid on the <strong>8-Down train</strong> traveling from Saharanpur to Lucknow as it approached the rural station of <strong>Kakori</strong> on August 9, 1925. They stopped the train and looted the British official treasury bag without harming any passengers.</p>\n\n    <h4>4. Kakori Conspiracy Case & Executions</h4>\n    <p>The colonial authorities unleashed draconian sweeps, arresting over 40 persons across North India. A defense committee headed by Pandit Motilal Nehru, Govind Ballabh Pant, and C.B. Gupta defended the patriots in court.</p>\n    <ul>\n        <li><strong>Martyrdom (December 1927):</strong> Four revolutionaries were condemned to the gallows:\n            <ul>\n                <li><strong>Ram Prasad Bismil</strong> was hanged in Gorakhpur Central Jail on December 19, 1927.</li>\n                <li><strong>Ashfaqulla Khan</strong> was hanged in Faizabad Jail on December 19, 1927.</li>\n                <li><strong>Roshan Singh</strong> was hanged in Naini Central Jail, Allahabad, on December 19, 1927.</li>\n                <li><strong>Rajendra Lahiri</strong> was hanged in Gonda Jail two days early on December 17, 1927.</li>\n            </ul>\n        </li>\n        <li><strong>Chandrashekhar Azad</strong> eluded police dragnets, remaining underground to rebuild the organization.</li>\n    </ul>\n</div>\n",
