                "Dharasana Salt Satyagraha (May 21, 1930): Following Gandhi's arrest on May 4, a non-violent raid on the Dharasana Salt Works was led by Sarojini Naidu, Imam Saheb, and Manilal Gandhi (Gandhi's son). American journalist Webb Miller documented the brutal police beatings of unarmed volunteers, horrifying world public opinion.",
