                "Sapru-Jayakar Peace Efforts: Moderate leaders Sir Tej Bahadur Sapru and M.R. Jayakar initiated mediation between the Viceroy and Congress leaders.",
                "Gandhi-Irwin Pact (Delhi Pact - March 5, 1931): Historic pact signed between Mahatma Gandhi and Viceroy Lord Irwin, placing the Congress on an equal bargaining footing with the colonial government.",
                "Pact Terms: Congress agreed to suspend the Civil Disobedience Movement and participate in the Second Round Table Conference; British agreed to immediately release all non-violent political prisoners, restore confiscated lands, permit peaceful picketing of liquor and foreign cloth shops, and allow coastal villagers to manufacture salt for personal consumption.",
                "Controversy over Bhagat Singh: Gandhi's inability to secure the commutation of the death sentences of Bhagat Singh, Sukhdev, and Rajguru sparked intense public fury, particularly among youth and leftists.",
                "Karachi Congress Session (March 29–31, 1931): Presided over by Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel, held just six days after the executions of Bhagat Singh, Rajguru, and Sukhdev. Youth presented black flags to Gandhi.",
